{
 "schema": "opentallas.s81_dv.bind_table.v2",
 "note": "S81-DIE5 (10-18) p4k bind table = p4j_b3 + the p4k plan lanes at the benched RTL widths: svc_rs faces (index = face N/E/S/W, unlinked faces tied as pads: the role ROM faults a word on a non-tree face), q 2 x 276 (slice bo[0] + bo[52 +: 512] -> entry q[512:0]; q[514:513] {fault, live} are not read by dsdv_svc_rs_c), P.V 562 {pv_d, pv_v} -> dsfd_dvland_pvrd (landing + static RD-beat adapter) -> slice bi, gunit cw, seqhost job (broadcast to both entries) and E-entry {jd, hc}; st_rg tied (pad, reason). | S81-BIND3 (10-17) p4j bind table: p4j_land + unit RTL from claude/s81-bind3-1017 (gunit s81u1/gunit3/native3-gunit, seq_host s81u-seq, svc_rs s81u-svc (+svcx4), bk vertical cut s81u2-bk, landing s81land2(+rly)). Half-cycle relays dsfd_dvrlyh_* (closed h1-41e90080d views). Straps marked 'bench value' are the unit bench values: the die values are owed by the compiler/plan table (owner in the residual table). S81-DV p4i REAL-RTL bind table (S81-DIE 10-17, from S81-BIND v1). module null = OPEN BINDING (no RTL; never stubbed), listed with its owner. Port map key = <plan endpoint port>.<o|i>; lane = RTL lane width; ck = the RTL forwarded-clock output used as hop-0 source. view = the CLOSED view the die binds (null = none yet). mode_unused = ports tied 0 because the mode is provably unused at that position (coordinator 0da (c)); each is declared to the strict check as a pad. | S81-DIE2 10-17: frames + ctrl_rg2 bound, all relay views closed, PHY face abutted. | S81-DIE4 10-17: 70-b relays + kp4 ddly/dout bound (native PASS); slice rt lanes without producer tied per 0cj (b). | S81-LAND2 10-17 (bind_table_p4j_land.json): p4j table + LANDINGS (dsfd_dvland_<W>, LANDING-CONTRACT) on the slice inputs ri_w / ri_e / vi / bi / rt and the dsfd_ctrl_rg2 rq input (port rule \"land\": true); K straps from land_plan (die STA pilot E, G = R0)",
